From 1fd91b90a7204c7846f2fc0580cc967a20d692cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:56:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: preserve occupied firmware routes before
 bypass probe

The firmware bypass test overwrites the last reliable S2CR before reading
valid SMRs, then may disable the last context bank even when a live
firmware route references it. A strict UEFI retirement also means USB
SID 0x40 cannot be assumed to supply an inherited bypass context.

Take a bounded raw SMR/S2CR/SCTLR snapshot before the first write. Reserve
referenced and enabled firmware CBs, retain every valid route, and probe
only an invalid SMR slot whose state is refreshed and restored. Allocate
an emulated bypass bank only from unreferenced, disabled stage1-capable
CBs, refresh routes before configuration and require CB readback. Refuse
full/unsupported geometry, state drift and failed restoration rather
than overwriting occupied hardware. Identity attachment still uses the
normal IOMMU path and can replace an inherited FAULT route.

Add shared snapshot selectors and host assertions for live M0 references,
enabled unreferenced banks, stage2 exclusion and exhausted geometry.
Both affected objects compile for AArch64 with the full candidate config;
the selector test passes ASAN/UBSAN. No device validation, ready marker,
USB-route cloning or global SMMU disable is included. DT master bindings,
secure access, global reset/TLB effects and real DMA remain to validate.

Based-on: 352508459733d3e6d349ea5581a8dd2fd8bb4180
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
